# Bitbucket Data Center 9.4.5 - Local POC Personal Access Token
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. Copy it to "bitbucket-token.txt" (no .example
# suffix) in this same directory and replace the placeholder below with a
# real Bitbucket Data Center HTTP access token.
#
# "bitbucket-token.txt" is covered by .gitignore and MUST NEVER be
# committed. This mechanism is for LOCAL POC USE ONLY -- see Section 12 /
# README.md "Production Hardening" for the enterprise replacement
# (OAuth/OIDC, GitHub App, Atlassian OAuth, secret manager, credential
# broker, managed/workload identity).
#
# Required scope: a Bitbucket HTTP access token with the minimum
# permissions needed for the operations you intend to exercise
# (read-only testing requires only repository read; write/admin testing
# requires the corresponding project/repository admin permission).
#
# Format: the raw token value, nothing else, no quotes, no trailing
# newline content beyond the token itself.
REPLACE_WITH_REAL_BITBUCKET_TOKEN
